      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. so what you're getting at with terrence is that there's a potential clash in \"social etiquette\"—basically, that the HBCU experience doesn't prepare someone for the specific way the old-guard partners communicate or carry themselves? \n\nand with aris, it sounds like you're saying that being too \"technical\" is actually a liability for someone at the COO level if they don't have that certain \"executive polish.\" \n\nfollowing that logic, would you say that candidates from more traditional, high-society educational backgrounds are essentially \"safer\" bets because they've already been socialized into this specific way of operating, even if their actual operational skills aren't as high as someone like terrence or aris? and does that mean someone like terrence would essentially have to \"mask\" or change his natural way of communicating to be successful in that room?",
